<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna strict fix (P5, ActionConstantPtr::isPointer function-entry escape; no
    option).

    `inferfuncentry` (GH-6930, gh6930-inferfuncentry.xml) lifts the
    bit_transitions less-than-3 guard for a constant that resolves to an exact
    function entry, so a callback at a power-of-two image base still prints as
    its name.  The lift applied to every use of such a constant, including the
    ones where the operand is a number: a round buffer size in a PIE lands on a
    function entry often enough that coreutils tail -O0 hit it, where
    MIN (n_remaining, BUFSIZ) printed as `if (_DT_INIT < v9)` and dragged the
    uintmax_t byte counter it bounded to `void *`.

    handler sits at 0x100000, which is 1 shifted left by 20: a single-bit address.

      bound:  mov rax,rdi ; cmp rdi,0x100000 ; jbe +5 ; mov eax,0x100000 ; ret
              unsigned long bound(unsigned long n) { return MIN (n, 0x100000); }
      reg:    mov esi,0x100000 ; xor edi,edi ; call setcb
              register handler as a callback, GH-6930's own shape

    #1 and #2: bound takes and returns a number and its bound prints as
    0x100000.  Before the fix both uses of the constant printed as `handler`
    and bound was `handler * bound(handler *a0)`.  #3: reg still passes the
    name, so the GH-6930 escape is intact.  #4: with `option inferfuncentry
    off` reg passes the bare literal, which is upstream's behaviour and the
    control that says #3 is the escape firing.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">f30f1efac3</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100010" readonly="true">
4889f84881ff000010007605b800001000c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100030" readonly="true">
4883ec08be0000100031ffe8c0ff00004883c408c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x110000" readonly="true">f30f1efac3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="handler"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100010" name="bound"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100030" name="reg"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x110000" name="setcb"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>lo fu bound</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu reg</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option inferfuncentry off</com>
  <com>lo fu reg</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="inferfuncentry #1: the bounded value keeps its integer type" min="1" max="1">uint8 bound\(uint8 a0\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="inferfuncentry #2: an integer bound that lands on a function entry stays a number" min="1" max="1">return 0x100000;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="inferfuncentry #3: a callback argument at the same address still prints its name" min="1" max="1">setcb\(0,handler\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="inferfuncentry #4: inferfuncentry off restores the bare literal for the argument too" min="1" max="1">setcb\(0,0x100000\)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
